.el .ds Aq '
.TH chronos-sentinel 1  "chronos-sentinel 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
chronos\-sentinel \- pacman integrity baseline (Arch)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBchronos\-sentinel\fR [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-pacman\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-full\-files\fR] [\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
pacman integrity baseline (Arch)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
show Byteflow audit: lines on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-json\fR
JSON log lines on stderr (or CHRONOS_LOG_JSON=1)
.TP
\fB\-\-pacman\-db\fR \fI<PACMAN_DB>\fR
Pacman local database (default: /var/lib/pacman/local on Linux)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
TOML config (else CHRONOS_CONFIG, XDG, /etc/chronos\-sentinel/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-full\-files\fR
Track every %FILES% path (default: usr/bin, usr/lib, etc/ssh, … prefixes only)
.TP
\fB\-\-state\-dir\fR \fI<STATE_DIR>\fR
Override state directory (else CHRONOS_STATE_DIR, XDG, or .chronos/)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-try(1)
Synthetic end\-to\-end run: on → status → off (uses \-d)
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-on(1)
Save baseline (state dir/baseline.json)
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-off(1)
Diff and verify against baseline
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-status(1)
Show baseline path / ON state
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-inventory(1)
Export inventory JSON (add \-d on Windows)
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-diff(1)
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-verify(1)
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-hash(1)
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-agent(1)
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-completions(1)
Print shell completion script to stdout
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-gen\-man(1)
Write roff man page to stdout or \-\-output
.TP
chronos\-sentinel\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Windows/dev:  chronos\-sentinel try     |     \-d = \-\-demo = \-\-dem
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
